//@ compile-fail
//@ error-pattern: error[E188]
//@ error-pattern: does not balance for element H
//@ error-pattern: element H: left 9, right 7
//@ error-pattern: element O: left 4, right 3
// NEGATIVE CONTROL. This is the sulfate-reduction reaction transcribed verbatim
// from the USGS AuxVases GWB script, which balances exactly (H 9/9, S 1/1,
// O 4/4, charge -1/-1), with ONE coefficient perturbed: `4 H2O` -> `3 H2O`.
//
// The point of the test is not merely that the checker rejects it. It is that
// the diagnostic NAMES the element and REPORTS BOTH COUNTS, so the author is
// told what is missing and by how much rather than only that something is
// wrong. Dropping one water removes 2 H and 1 O, so H must read 9 vs 7 and O
// must read 4 vs 3 — both are pinned above. S still balances and must NOT be
// reported.

reaction sulfate_reduction_perturbed {
    4 H2(aq) + H+ + SO4-- -> HS- + 3 H2O
}

fn main() with IO {
    println("unreachable")
}
